> What's green goo? What are smart contracts? (I thought that one of
> the virtues of a contract was being stupid enough not to change itself.)

I guess this is an example of "lack of list memory" that Tim May
often complains about, as I've posted essays on both of these 
to exi-essay, and they've been widely commented on here and elsewhere.

"Green Goo" are parasites released by eco-terrorists for the purposes 
of population control.  This is already being done in Australia with 
other mammal species, and there are several options for bioengineering 
viruses that would depopulate humans to the level desired by many ecofascists,
either by sterility (the "humane genocide" scenario that is much more
easily justified in the minds of many ecofascists, thus more probable), 
or outright death.  This scenario is vastly more probable than the 
silly "gray goo" scenario.

Smart contracts are contracts implemented with software that
are self-auditing, self-enforcing, etc.  They will be used to
construct new kinds of property rights, and indeed new economic
and political institutions, in cyberspace.  If you can access the 
netcom web server try 
	ftp://ftp.netcom.com/pub/sz/szabo/home.html
for Smart Contracts and other essays of mine.  (Alas, I've lost
my Green Goo essay in my labyrinth of backups, if anybody has
a copy handy to send back to me it would be greatly appreciated).

